# Form Validation Pattern

## Rules at a Glance

- Validation logic lives in the **domain layer** as a synchronous usecase
- The validation usecase does **not** extend the async `UseCase<T, P>` base class — it is infallible and returns a result directly
- The BLoC calls the validation usecase **before** dispatching to the action usecase
- `ValidationResult` extends `Equatable` — it is stored in BLoC state `props`
- The widget has **no validator lambdas** — it dispatches events only

---

## File Locations

```
features/<feature>/
  domain/
    usecases/
      validate_<action>_input_usecase.dart   ← synchronous, no Future, no ApiResponse
    value_objects/
      <action>_validation_result.dart        ← Equatable, field-level errors + isValid
  presentation/
    bloc/
      <feature>_bloc.dart                    ← calls validation before action usecase
      <feature>_state.dart                   ← includes a ValidationFailed state
```

---

## ValidationResult — Equatable Domain Class

```dart
// domain/value_objects/login_validation_result.dart
class LoginValidationResult extends Equatable {
  final String? emailError;
  final String? passwordError;

  const LoginValidationResult({this.emailError, this.passwordError});

  bool get isValid => emailError == null && passwordError == null;

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [emailError, passwordError];
}
```

---

## ValidationUseCase — Synchronous, No Base Class

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT — standalone class, synchronous call(), no Future, no ApiResponse
class ValidateLoginInputUseCase {
  LoginValidationResult call({required String email, required String password}) {
    return LoginValidationResult(
      emailError: _validateEmail(email),
      passwordError: _validatePassword(password),
    );
  }

  String? _validateEmail(String value) { ... }
  String? _validatePassword(String value) { ... }
}

// ❌ WRONG — do not extend the async UseCase base class
class ValidateLoginInputUseCase extends UseCase<LoginValidationResult, LoginParams> {
  Future<ApiResponse<LoginValidationResult>> call(LoginParams params) async { ... }
}
```

---

## BLoC — Validate Before Action Dispatch

Add a `<Feature>ValidationFailed` state and call the validation usecase at the top of the action handler.

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT — validate first, then proceed
Future<void> _onAuthLoginRequested(
  AuthLoginRequested event,
  Emitter<AuthState> emit,
) async {
  final validation = _validateLoginInputUseCase(
    email: event.email,
    password: event.password,
  );

  if (!validation.isValid) {
    emit(AuthValidationFailed(validation));
    return;
  }

  emit(AuthLoading());
  final response = await _loginUseCase(
    LoginParams(email: event.email, password: event.password),
  );
  switch (response) {
    case ApiSuccess(:final data): emit(AuthAuthenticated(data));
    case ApiError(:final message): emit(AuthError(message));
  }
}
```

```dart
// <feature>_state.dart — add a ValidationFailed state per action
class AuthValidationFailed extends AuthState {
  final LoginValidationResult result;
  const AuthValidationFailed(this.result);

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [result];
}
```

---

## Widget — No Validator Lambdas

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT — widget reads errors from state; BLoC owns validation
AppTextField(
  controller: _emailController,
  label: AppStrings.email,
  errorText: state is AuthValidationFailed ? state.result.emailError : null,
),

// ❌ WRONG — validation logic inside widget
AppTextField(
  validator: (value) {
    if (value == null || value.isEmpty) return 'Required';
    // ...
  },
),
```

Remove `GlobalKey<FormState>` — it is not needed when validation is owned by the BLoC.

---

## DI Registration

```dart
// core/di/<feature>_injection.dart
sl.registerLazySingleton(() => ValidateLoginInputUseCase());

sl.registerFactory(() => AuthBloc(
  validateLoginInputUseCase: sl(),
  loginUseCase: sl(),
  // ...
));
```

`ValidationUseCase` is stateless — `registerLazySingleton` is correct.

---

## Unit Test

```dart
final usecase = ValidateLoginInputUseCase();

test('isValid false when email is missing @', () {
  final result = usecase(email: 'notanemail', password: 'secret123');
  expect(result.emailError, AppStrings.invalidEmail);
  expect(result.isValid, isFalse);
});

test('isValid true for well-formed input', () {
  final result = usecase(email: 'a@b.com', password: 'secret123');
  expect(result.isValid, isTrue);
});
```

---

## ❌ Violations

- Inline validator lambdas inside any widget
- Validation logic inside a Repository, DataSource, or `ApiClient`
- `ValidationUseCase` extending the async `UseCase<T, P>` base class
- Using `_formKey.currentState?.validate()` when a `ValidationUseCase` exists for the form
- `ValidationResult` without `Equatable` (it lives in BLoC state `props`)
- Emitting `AuthLoading` before validating — validation must happen first, synchronously
